plugin-db-qualification (2026112001) unstable; urgency=medium

  * An absent base is an empty base layer (#36): the reader opens with no
    base, says so in one stderr line, and pqdb_base_absent reports it;
    only ENOENT counts as absent.
  * The records are a sqlite base built from records/ (#25): the base build
    checks every word against its owner's domain, gives a cell to the
    reference tier whatever the set order, and to the set measured later
    within one tier; the console profile's verdicts are held back (#5).
  * The real-time reference sets of #5 join as fedora44-rt-<cell> (22
    sets), with the non-real-time 192000/128 run and the Raspberry Pi
    re-measure as sets of their own (#38, Fixes #5); records go in the
    byte order of their whole paths (#39).
  * The other-threads grid uses the producer's short names (#35), and the
    development package depends on sqlite's (#34).
  * The symbols file names pqdb_base_absent, and a test holds the file to
    the header.
  * The release proof takes the base database beside the classes for the
    base, not for a class, and refuses a package without it (#41, #42).
  * The release proof names plugin-hostd's settings file with hostd_conf
    and writes the plugin folders there, not in qualify.conf (#43, #45).
  * The records depend on plugin-qualify 0.20.7 or later on every
    architecture (#46, #47).
  * plugin-qualification-db query --json --records takes --rate and
    --quantum and prints the record that claims that cell, with its set;
    every --records line names its set (#54, #55).
  * The release proof compares the set plugin-qualify-sync takes at each
    cell with the store's claim, and installs the channel's omx-plugins
    (#51, #52, #53). Under plugin-qualify 0.20.7, which takes the first set
    by name: on rpi5 zynthian-vangelis-48000-256 and -96000-256 are never
    taken (zynthian-vangelis is taken at their cells, a wrong winner until
    plugin-qualify 0.20.8, #152); on x86-64 the 33 sets' 1056 omx-plugins
    records are unproven, measured with omx-plugins 0.19.1, which the
    channel no longer serves (the channel serves 0.19.3).

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:39:24 +0100

plugin-db-qualification (2026111901) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The qualification store's C reader, libplugin-qualification-db0, and its
    command plugin-qualification-db, widened to the store spec (#22, #28):
    binary_path and layer in queries, the audit fields and history tables,
    numbers in JSON.stringify layout under a per-thread C locale, a
    non-finite REAL refused as not-a-store, pqdb_message and pqdb_number.
  * The writer, plugin-qualification-db-write, and the schema package,
    plugin-qualification-db-schema (#27): the user and system layers from
    records, every word checked against its owner's installed domain.
  * Hosting words this pass (#30): the writer reads them from the installed
    omx-clap-core contract package; the reader passes over them, and
    hosting-skip-ends holds the end of that exception.
  * The store spec (#16, #20, #21, #23, #26) and the Fedora 45 rpms (#24,
    #29). The records package's records are unchanged.

